# Database schema

- database/schema.sql is the sole DDL authority: tables, columns, defaults, enums, constraints, indexes, triggers and comments. Do not add a second schema or generated mapping.
- Use pg through lib/database/client.ts and explicit domain repositories in lib/database/repositories. Bind external values with the sql tag; identifiers must come from reviewed static code.
- Follow 05-record-identifiers.mdc: BIGINT identity PK/FKs and immutable database-generated UUIDv4 public_id. Explicit public DTOs contain UUIDs only.
- Keep bigint and numeric values exact: internal IDs use bigint; DECIMAL(65,30) uses strings. Never coerce stored numeric values through Number for persistence or sums.
- Date-only and timestamp values represent Asia/Bangkok calendar/wall-clock values. Use the shared parsers and serializers; host/browser timezone must not alter storage.
- Keep SQL status/theme values hyphenated: in-progress, sa-testing, pm-testing, special-dark.
- Company is required on Project. Daily Work creates require an owned WorkItem and derive its numeric project_id server-side. Retain restrictive history guards.
- External source IDs remain separate from local identities. issue_sync_configs.token_env_var names a server .env token variable; never store token values in a table.
- Initialize schema.sql only on an empty approved target. Existing mismatched schemas are refused. Validate SQL against disposable databases; preserve live data and private seeds.
